Hey folks, hi @wesm 👋 !

I can confirm the diagnosis from a separate `pg serve` deployment — same symptom, same root cause (`messages.id == 0` from the PG path → duplicate keys in `ToolCallGroup`'s outer each).

One small wrinkle on the suggested fixes:

The PG `messages` table has no `id` column today — `internal/postgres/schema.go:72-100` defines the PK as `(session_id, ordinal)` with no surrogate id. So just adding `id, ` to the two SELECTs would fail at query time; a non-destructive migration adding `id BIGSERIAL` (or equivalent) would have to land first.
Also, Frontend `source_uuid` keying isn't safe across agents: `source_uuid` is `DEFAULT ''` in the schema but only Claude populates it. Non-Claude sessions (Codex, Copilot, Gemini, Forge, etc.) leave it empty, so multiple tool-using messages would key on `""` and re-trigger the same error.

The smallest correct fix for the render crash, across both backends and every agent, is keying this local message loop on `ordinal`, which is already part of the PG PK and populated everywhere:

```svelte
{#each messages as message (message.ordinal)}
```

...but then `ToolCallGroup`'s duration lookup should join timing by ordinal too. PG timing intentionally synthesizes `turns[].message_id` from the message ordinal because PG has no message `id` column, while the messages API still emits `id: 0`. SQLite, on the other hand, emits the real surrogate id as `turns[].message_id`, so keeping `message_id` as the timing-map key can't work uniformly across both backends.

So the frontend patch I'm testing is:

```svelte
let turnByOrdinal = $derived.by(() => {
  const m = new Map<number, TurnTiming>();
  for (const t of sessionTiming.timing?.turns ?? []) {
    m.set(t.ordinal, t);
  }
  return m;
});

{#each messages as message (message.ordinal)}
  {@const turn = turnByOrdinal.get(message.ordinal)}
```

That addresses both the duplicate-key crash and the `ToolCallGroup` duration badges. Same ordinal-join principle may also apply to the remaining `MessageContent.svelte` timing lookups for non-grouped tool-call badges/turn chips to be correct in `pg serve`.

Happy to send a PR with this frontend fix if it's useful?
